"Internal Error ()\nciteturn11view0 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://laws.justice.gc.ca/eng/regulations/SOR-2008-117/20080702/FullText.html\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 1\nL0: URL https://laws.justice.gc.ca/eng/regulations/SOR-2008-117/20080702/FullText.html is not accessible via this tool.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nIdentifying designated public office holders; | Office of the Commissioner of Lobbying of Canada (https://lobbycanada.gc.ca/en/rules/the-lobbying-act/advice-and-interpretation-lobbying-act/identifying-designated-public-office-holders/)\nciteturn11view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 days ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://lobbycanada.gc.ca/en/rules/the-lobbying-act/advice-and-interpretation-lobbying-act/identifying-designated-public-office-holders/\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 70\nL0:   * cite0†Skip to main content L1:   * cite1†Skip to \"About this site\" L2: \nL3: ## Language selection\nL4: \nL5:   * cite2†Sign in to Registry L6:   * cite3†Français L7: \nL8: ## Menu\nL9: \nL10: Main Menu\nL11: \nL12: Search website [Input: Search website]\nL13: \nL14: Search\nL15: # Identifying designated public office holders\nL16: \nL17: The term “designated public office holder”, which is defined in subsection cite4†2(1)†laws-lois.justice.gc.ca of the Lobbying Act, is important for two main reasons.\nL18: First, registered consultant lobbyists and the senior officer responsible for filing returns are required to report, on a monthly basis, cite5†oral and arranged communications†laws-lois.justice.gc.ca with designated public office holders on behalf of their clients or employers regarding any of the matters listed in paragraph cite6†5(1)(a)†laws-lois.justice.gc.ca or cite7†7(1)(a)†laws-lois.justice.gc.ca , as applicable.\nL19: Second, all former designated public office holders are subject to the five-year restriction on lobbying set out in subsection cite8†10.11(1)†laws-lois.justice.gc.ca of the Lobbying Act.\nL20: The purpose of this interpretation bulletin is to identify the categories of officials who qualify as designated public office holders and to explain how the Office of the Commissioner of Lobbying interprets the term “comparable rank” in the definition of “designated public office holder” at subparagraph 2(1)(b)(ii) of the Lobbying Act and the term “equivalent rank” in paragraphs 127.1(1)(a) and (b) of the Public Service Employment Act.\nL21: ## Identified designated public office holders\nL22: \nL23: The Lobbying Act and the cite9†Designated Public Office Holder Regulations†laws-lois.justice.gc.ca identify who qualifies as a designated public office holder.\nL24: \nL25: Lobbying Act  | Designated Public Office Holder Regulations\nL26: --- | ---\nL27: The Lobbying Act identifies the following categories of individuals as designated public office holders:\nL28:   * ministers and ministers of state and members of their respective ministerial staff;\nL29:   * officials occupying the following positions in a “department” as defined in section cite10†2†laws-lois.justice.gc.ca and listed in cite11†Schedule I†laws-lois.justice.gc.ca , cite12†column 1 of Schedule I.1†laws-lois.justice.gc.ca or cite13†Schedule II†laws-lois.justice.gc.ca of the Financial Administration Act:\nL30:     * the senior executive position, whether by the title of deputy minister, Chief Executive Officer or by another title; and\nL31:     * associate and assistant deputy minister as well as positions of cite14†“comparable rank” L32:   * officials occupying a position designated by regulation (see right hand column); and\nL33:   * members of a transition team providing advice to the Prime Minister during the period leading up to the swearing in of the Prime Minister.\nL34:  | The Regulations identify the following categories of individuals as designated public office holders:\nL35:   * Senators and Members of the House of Commons;\nL36:   * officials appointed under paragraph cite15†127.1(1)(a) or (b)†laws-lois.justice.gc.ca of the Public Service Employment Act to the position of:\nL37:     * deputy minister or associate deputy minister or to a position of cite14†“equivalent rank” (s. 127.1(1)(a)); or\nL38:     * deputy head or associate deputy head or to a position of cite14†“equivalent rank” (s. 127.1(1)(b))\nL39:   * senior advisors of the Privy Council appointed by the Governor in Council;\nL40:   * staff members to the Leader of the Opposition in the Senate and House of Commons appointed under subsection cite16†128(1)†laws-lois.justice.gc.ca of the Public Service Employment Act;\nL41:   * the Deputy Minister (Intergovernmental Affairs) of the Privy Council Office;\nL42:   * the Comptroller General;\nL43:   * the Chief and Vice Chief of the Defence Staff;\nL44:   * the Chiefs of the Maritime, Land and Air Staff;\nL45:   * the Chief of Military Personnel; and\nL46:   * the Judge Advocate General.\nL47: ## Interpreting “comparable rank” and “equivalent rank”\nL48: \nL49: In determining whether a given official qualifies as a designated public office holder on the basis that:\nL50:   * the position they occupy is of “comparable rank” to that of an associate or assistant deputy minister (subparagraph 2(1)(b)(ii) of the Lobbying Act); or\nL51:   * the position to which they have been appointed is of “equivalent rank” to either that of a deputy or associate deputy minister or that of a deputy or associate deputy head (paragraph 127.1(1)(a) or (b) of the Public Service Employment Act)\nL52: the Office of the Commissioner of Lobbying engages in a contextual analysis that takes into account the following non-exhaustive list of factors:\nL53: \nL54:   * the seniority or rank of the position;\nL55:   * the responsibilities and decision-making authority of the position; and\nL56:   * the pay range associated with the position.\nL57: In practice, occupying a position in the first, second or third highest level of a government institution’s hierarchy and/or whose pay range is similar to that of an EX-04 are both strong indications that an official’s position may be comparable to that of an associate or assistant deputy minister or of equivalent rank to that of a deputy or associate deputy minister or deputy head or associate deputy head, as applicable.\nL58: That said, no single factor is determinative of the comparable or equivalent rank analysis described above and the outcome of this analysis will always depend on all of the relevant factual circumstances.\nL59: ## Ask the Office of the Commissioner of Lobbying\nL60: \nL61: Contact our Office to confirm whether an official qualifies as a designated public office holder.\nL62: \nL63: Nancy Bélanger\nL64: Commissioner of Lobbying\nL65: \nL66: September 2024\nL67: \nL68: Date modified:\nL69:     2026-07-16\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nW8703-270094 Low-Cost Uncrewed Aircraft Systems (UAS) RFP-A - Tender Notice | CanadaBuys (https://canadabuys.canada.ca/en/tender-opportunities/tender-notice/ws5853743341-doc5853864815)\nciteturn11view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 days ago; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn10view0\",\"id\":11}); Total lines: 250\nL0: Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website.\nL1: \nL2:   * cite0†Skip to main content L3:   * cite1†Skip to \"About Canada.ca\" L4: \nL5: ## Language selection\nL6: \nL7:   * cite2†fr (Français) L8: \nL9: Search CanadaBuys [Input: Search CanadaBuys]\nL10: \nL11: Search\nL12: \nL13: ## Canada.ca Menu\nL14: \nL15: Main Menu\nL16: \nL17: ## Buy Canadian Policy\nL18: \nL19: The Government of Canada has introduced new policies to protect, build, and transform Canadian industries. Check out cite3†Buy Canadian Policy for more information on what this could mean for you.\nL20: # W8703-270094 Low-Cost Uncrewed Aircraft Systems (UAS) RFP-A\nL21: \nL22: Solicitation number WS5853743341\nL23: \nL24: Publication date 2026/08/27\nL25: \nL26: Closing date and time 2026/09/03 14:00 EDT\nL27: \nL28: Last amendment date 2026/09/03\nL29: \nL30: Status Status Expired\nL31: \nL32: cite4†Create a notification to follow this noticeFollow this notice L33: \nL34: cite5†How to bookmark this noticeBookmark this notice L35: \nL36: * * *\nL37: \nL38: [Input] Description\nL39: ATTENTION: All required supporting documentation and bid submission must be submitted by 03 September 2026 by 14:00 EDT. All bids submitted after 14:00 EDT will result in the bid being declared non-responsive.\nL40: Canada is seeking offers from Offerors to provide Complex Terrain Uncrewed Ground Vehicle (CT-UGV) systems, including associated spare parts, support equipment, documentation, training, sustainment, and related support services to the Department of National Defence (DND) and the Canadian Armed Forces (CAF). The CT-UGV systems are intended to support tactical load carriage and operational experimentation in complex terrain environments.\nL41: This is a Request for Proposal only for Holders of Supply Arrangement W8703-270055 Defence Drone Initiative (DDI) Marketplace Stream 1. If other offerors are interested in submitting a proposal they will have to qualify for Supply Arrangement before they are given an opportunity to submit an offer on this requirement. Canada will not extend this RFP to provide additional time for bidders to qualify for the Supply Arrangement and submit a proposal for this RFP.\nL42: Show more description   Show less description\nL43: ### Contract duration\nL44: \nL45: Refer to the description above for full details.\nL46: \nL47: ### Trade agreements\nL48: \nL49:   * No trade agreements are applicable to this solicitation process\nL50: \nL51: ### Reason for limited tendering\nL52: \nL53: A contracting officer can use limited tendering for specific reasons outlined in the applicable trade agreements. The reason for this contract is described below:\nL54: \nL55:   * None\nL56: \nL57: cite6†Image L58: ## Partner with another business\nL59: \nL60: Are you interested in partnering with other businesses for this opportunity? cite7†Add your company to the list of businesses who are interested in partnering .\nL61: \nL62: This list does not replace or affect the tendering procedures for this procurement process. Businesses are still required to respond to bid solicitations, and to compete based on the set criteria. cite8†For more information please read the Terms of use .\nL63: Businesses interested in partnering for this tender opportunity:\nL64: Note: Information may not be available in both English and French. This is because the Official Languages Act does not apply.\nL65: \nL66:   * cite9†Immervision Inc. L67: \nL68:   * cite10†SectorNorth Battlefield Solutions Inc. L69: \nL70:   * cite11†Tactix Procurement Advisors L71: \nL72:   * cite12†First Class Drones Inc. L73: \nL74: Contact information\nL75: ### Contracting organization\nL76: \nL77: Organization\nL78: \nL79: \nL80: \nL81: Department of Public Works and Government Services (PSPC)\nL82: \nL83: Address\nL84: \nL85: \nL86: \nL87: 11 Laurier St, Phase III, Place du Portage\nL88: \nL89: Gatineau, Quebec, K1A 0S5\nL90: \nL91: Canada\nL92: \nL93: Contracting authority\nL94: \nL95: \nL96: \nL97: Murphy, Heather (SPAC/PSPC) (elle-la / she-her)\nL98: \nL99: Email\nL100: \nL101: \nL102: \nL103: heather.murphy@tpsgc-pwgsc.gc.ca\nL104: ### Buying organization(s)\nL105: \nL106: Organization\nL107: \nL108: \nL109: \nL110: Department of National Defence (DND)\nL111: \nL112: Address\nL113: \nL114: \nL115: \nL116: 101 Colonel By Dr\nL117: \nL118: Ottawa, Ontario, K1A0K2\nL119: \nL120: Canada\nL121: \nL122: Bidding details\nL123: \nL124: All details for this tender opportunity are provided in the cite13†Description tab. No additional solicitation documents are available to download.\nL125: \nL126: C